libeasymcp2221++ (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Prepare the 0.2.0 release.
  * Add optional Qt 6 integration and Qt Debian packages.
  * Add Windows MSVC and MinGW-w64 support.
  * Add binary release packaging and installed-package consumer tests.
  * Harden shared-library visibility and Debian ABI symbol tracking.
  * Fix static installed-package linkage and make Windows SDKs self-contained.
  * Align flash, GPIO, validation, and ownership behavior with the C library.
  * Require libeasymcp2221 2.0.2 for the final 0.2.0 release.

 -- Tobias X. Vogel <tobias.vogel@linux.com>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 20:30:00 +0200

